OL,3,GNEWSA'We lost her future': Family's
OL,4,Abrain tumour plea
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe family of a woman who died from a
OL,7,Fbrain tumour say they want to see more
OL,8,Fnational cancer fundraising directed
OL,9,Ftowards brain tumour research.
OL,11,FEvanne Miller-Bettridge, from Tamworth,
OL,12,Fdied in April 2025, aged 24, after
OL,13,Fbeing diagnosed with a malignant tumour
OL,14,Fin 2019.
OL,16,FHer father, Greg Hughes, said: "We feel
OL,17,Fthe need for national funding is so
OL,18,Fimportant, because as a disease it
OL,19,Foverly affects young people.
OL,23,APub: 26-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,359,350,200,160,0,100
